# =============================================================================
#  LINE ENDINGS -- one stated convention
# =============================================================================
#  Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true in the SYSTEM config, which is why
#  every `git add` warned. Declaring the convention here makes a byte
#  comparison between two checkouts mean something.
#
#  Related, though not fixed by this file: ETHICS.md was once UTF-8 text
#  re-encoded as latin-1 (4 middots, 9 em-dashes, a BOM, and a broken
#  o-umlaut in "Mobius"). Line endings and character encoding are different
#  problems; this file only settles the first. Write UTF-8, no BOM.
# =============================================================================

* text=auto eol=lf

# --- research payload: binary, never converted, never text-diffed -----------
*.h5      binary
*.pdf     binary
*.mp4     binary
*.zip     binary
*.tar.gz  binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary

# --- numerical data: ASCII tables, kept LF so diffs are real ----------------
*.dat  text eol=lf

*.svg  text eol=lf
